{"repositoryId":444993699,"availability":"available","full":"quant-daddy/graphql-eventbus","name":"graphql-eventbus","description":"GraphQL layer to publish and consume events from any message broker","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":26,"forks":1,"created":"2022-01-06T00:45:02Z","updated":"2026-09-18T06:38:52Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://graphql-eventbus.vercel.app","topics":["event-driven-microservices","eventbus","eventhub","graphql","pubsub","rabbitmq","sns","sqs"],"demo":"https://graphql-eventbus.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:32.335Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:32.335Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:32.335Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T02:48:32.335Z","stars":26,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["GraphQL eventbus is an abstraction layer on top of GraphQL SDL to publish and consume messages in a type-safe way. It is message broker agnotic: you can use Kafka, RabbitMQ, Google Pubsub or any other message broker. With features like code generation, API evolution without breaking changes, plugin system for logging and monitoring, and more, you can build a production quality event hub for your service architecture."],"features":["✂️ Schema Driven: Define your events and payloads in GraphQL schema. Consume your events using GraphQL documents.","🤝 Message Broker agnostic: Works with any message broker. We provide packages for Google Pubsub and RabbitMQ. You can easily use the library to build a bus for your message broker.","🚀 Code Generation: GraphQL Codegen","plugin to generate code for typescript (npm i graphql-eventbus-codegen).","🎯 Plugins: We provide plugins for logging and monitoring. You can also build your custom plugins."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/quant-daddy/graphql-eventbus/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"efa70be691f1c05c7591478afd5b7599e299a293738e859b08a3ea8f50e1360e","extractedAt":"2026